      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/e76766c18330d476af9253ecb2d08540df06146a9ac2fdc6bfbe6f8157201f6b.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the ray shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The counterclockwise angle that the ray makes with the positive $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{6\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is $\\theta =\\frac{6\\pi }{5}.$",
