  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-120704",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d90b9572-cdac-51f7-b386-81b750642585",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Polar Equation of a Radial Line That Passes Through a Given Point",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/03814c00b9e29f8a05507616ed08e3fe3daa484336e461012dc6c80799efc9e0.png)\n\nGiven that the ray above passes through the point with Cartesian coordinates $(-\\sqrt{6},-\\sqrt{2})$, find the polar equation of the ray.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{-\\sqrt{6}}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the third quadrant. So, we find the angle in the third quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{8}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\theta =\\frac{6\\pi }{5}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
