  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-77543",
      "knowledge_point_id": "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane",
      "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${A}^{′}$, the image of $A(-1,1)$ under the action of $T?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the image of $A$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $A:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${A}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${A}^{′}(2,1).$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-2,1)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(2,1)",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
